bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27, 2, "2026-11-27 follow-up: a direct Some(<f64>) argument (HIR types the call ANY) also crosses as a float (Rust test jit_direct_f64_some_literal_binds_float_through_untyped_parameter; probe base 3, fix 1). Other routes on seed 193d6b67d690b318 equal the interpreter: h(mk()), generic id<T>(a), method with an untyped param, and relay(a) back into f64? read by unwrap / if val / typed match (base: unwrap and if val false). Perf (2e7 boxed Some args of 4e7 calls): 7.05/5.44/5.53s, 672-679 MB vs base 0.25/0.23/0.28s, 41 MB with wrong values; base plain-f64 control pays 4e7 boxes at 31.6s / 1.3 GB, so the per-box cost is at parity (seed_jit_erased_float_arg_heap_box_per_call_never_released_2026-11-27). Design call open: raw-form construction of explicit f64? Some (seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27) would likely subsume this boundary conversion."
    seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-erasedf64 fix (work/bug-erased-f64-none-20261127): an f64?/Option<f64> argument bound to an erased (ANY) parameter is handed over in the raw f64? form. coerce_args_for_param_slots (mir/lower/lowering_expr_call.rs) emits, for such an arg: if rt_enum_check_variant(v, 1, Some) then BoxFloat(Cast F64->F64 of rt_enum_payload(v)) else v (nil / None / already-raw pass through). Typed f64? params, other box_arg_for_any_param callers and non-f64 optionals are unchanged. Red->green: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs jit_explicit_f64_option_some_binds_float_through_untyped_parameter 31400 -> 11411, jit_explicit_option_f64_some_binds_float_through_untyped_parameter 34 -> 14, jit_f64_option_boundary_in_caller_with_parameters 346 -> 146; native_project tests.rs erased_f64_option_some_boundary_survives_runtime_name_qualification abort -> 144. Seed f391cc81a8b1f257: probe f1 JIT S1.5 S2.5 N 1.75 S7 = interpreter (base S576179277326712832 ... 576179277326712800.0). Cost: each such call heap-boxes one float (rt_value_float); 4e7 erased calls 5.9-9.9s / 670 MB RSS vs base 0.24s (wrong values) -- the same price base already pays for a plain f64 into an untyped param (31.6s / 1.3 GB for 4e7 calls), filed as seed_jit_erased_float_arg_heap_box_per_call_never_released_2026-11-27. Residuals NOT fixed here: user enum f64 payload through an untyped binder (enum Ef: Some(f64); Ef.Some(0.1) -> JIT 3, interp 1), generic Bi<f64>.Some(0.5) (JIT 3, interp 1), f32? Some(0.5) (JIT 3, interp 1) -- the enum payload slot keeps raw float bits and an erased reader cannot know the type; needs the primitive-T? representation lane."

